                                    <div  id="collapseFaq_Faq" class="faq-body accordion-content collapse" aria-labelledby="heading_Faq" data-bs-parent="#accordion">                                            
                                           <p>&bull; When should juridical persons register for Corporate Tax?<br />
All juridical persons subject to Corporate Tax are required to register with the Federal Tax Authority and obtain a Corporate Tax Registration Number in accordance with the provisions of the <a href="https://tax.gov.ae/Datafolder/Files/Legislation/FTA Decision No. 3 of 2024 on Registration Timeline for Corporate Tax - For publishing.pdf">Federal Tax Authority Decision No. (3) of 2024</a> regarding the specified timeline for the registration of persons subject to Corporate Tax and Business Tax.</p>
<p>&bull; When should natural persons register for Corporate Tax?<br />
Natural persons are required to register for Corporate Tax if they conduct a business or business activity in the United Arab Emirates and their annual revenues exceed the registration threshold specified under the Corporate Tax Law. Registration must be completed within the prescribed timeframe in accordance with the <a href="https://tax.gov.ae/Datafolder/Files/Legislation/FTA Decision No. 3 of 2024 on Registration Timeline for Corporate Tax - For publishing.pdf">Federal Tax Authority Decision No. (3) of 2024</a> regarding the specified timeline for the registration of persons subject to Corporate Tax and Business Tax.</p>
<p>&bull; Is there a penalty for late registration for Corporate Tax? What is the amount, if applicable?<br />
Yes, an administrative penalty of AED 10,000 is imposed for late registration for Corporate Tax.</p>
<p>&bull; What is the Corporate Tax Late Registration Penalty Waiver Initiative?<br />
The Corporate Tax Late Registration Penalty Waiver Initiative allows taxable persons to be exempted from the AED 10,000 administrative penalty, provided that they submit their first Tax Return (or Annual Declaration for exempt persons, where applicable) within 7 months from the end of their first tax period.<br />
The initiative applies to persons who registered late, have not yet submitted a registration application, or have been charged the penalty regardless of whether it has been paid. If the penalty has already been paid, the amount will be credited back to the taxpayer&rsquo;s tax account upon meeting the conditions of the initiative.</p>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
                                            <div class="clear10"></div>                                                                             
                                    </div>
                                </div>

                                  
                               
                                 <div class="faq-item accordion-item">
